{
  "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
  "document_hash": "83d1c17d9199bb6e555b2c79159bbd21bd05990a8832c10914f399793858a31f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83d1c17d9199bb6e555b2c79159bbd21bd05990a8832c10914f399793858a31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83d1c17d9199-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83d1c17d9199bb6e555b2c79159bbd21bd05990a8832c10914f399793858a31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83d1c17d9199-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Department of Commerce, which is the Federal agency entrusted by Congress with the administration of the antidumping duty law, concluded after an extensive investigation that SWU contracts do result in sales of enriched uranium. That determination was reasonable and should be sustained by this Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Utilities and Enricher",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83d1c17d9199bb6e555b2c79159bbd21bd05990a8832c10914f399793858a31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83d1c17d9199-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Secondly, just about the specific situation here, I don't believe that there is any chance that the utilities and the enricher in this case could claim unfair surprise or unjust reliance; because they say in their own briefs, they did not set their transactions up in this way in order to try to comply with prior decisions of Commerce. They say -- they make a point in their brief in saying we have perfectly innocent intentions here, that they set their transactions up purely for historical and commercial reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83d1c17d9199bb6e555b2c79159bbd21bd05990a8832c10914f399793858a31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83d1c17d9199-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So -- now, the other question that Justice Breyer raises is about the cases, and Justice Ginsburg I think mentioned earlier the Florida Power & Light decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Farr (Commerce)",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83d1c17d9199bb6e555b2c79159bbd21bd05990a8832c10914f399793858a31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83d1c17d9199-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FARR: Well, I think -- the narrowest interpretation, and it seems to me the one that is most readily dealt with is, to say, in a situation where a customer provides raw material that is the type of, but not the precise raw material, used by a manufacturer to make the good that it then delivers to the customer, in that situation, we are going to treat the manufacturer as having made a sale of that good for the consideration of the cash and the raw material."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83d1c17d9199bb6e555b2c79159bbd21bd05990a8832c10914f399793858a31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83d1c17d9199-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "LEU. And the idea that the Respondents posit is, well, this is just a service performed on our material. All we are doing is getting our material back after a service has been performed on it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83d1c17d9199bb6e555b2c79159bbd21bd05990a8832c10914f399793858a31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83d1c17d9199-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Say it again?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. HALLIGAN",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "83d1c17d9199bb6e555b2c79159bbd21bd05990a8832c10914f399793858a31f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-83d1c17d9199-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. HALLIGAN: But the question, Your Honor, is -- is the price at which the product is sold in the United States. Section 1677(a) defines \"export price\" and \"constructed export price\" as the price at which the subject merchandise is first sold in the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2008-07-1059",
